## Project
<App name> — <one sentence: what it does and for whom>.
Full idea and scope: docs/app-idea.md

## Stack
- Frontend: Svelte 5 + Vite (frontend/)
- Backend: Node.js LTS + Express, ES modules (backend/)
- Database: PostgreSQL 17 via `pg`; schema managed by node-pg-migrate (backend/migrations/, SQL files)
- Runtime: Docker Compose (docker-compose.yml), config from .env

## Commands
- Start everything: `docker compose up -d --build`
- Logs: `docker compose logs -f backend`
- Backend tests: `cd backend && npm test`
- Frontend tests: `cd frontend && npm test`
- E2E: `cd frontend && npm run test:e2e`
- New migration: `cd backend && npx node-pg-migrate create <name> --migration-file-language sql`
- Apply migrations: `cd backend && npm run migrate up` (backend container also runs this on start)

## Coding rules
- Use async/await; no callbacks.
- Always use parameterized SQL queries (`$1, $2`); never build SQL with string concatenation.
- Validate and sanitize every request body/query on the backend.
- Return JSON errors as `{ "error": "<message>" }` with a correct HTTP status.
- Read secrets and config only from environment variables. Never hard-code secrets.
- Keep changes small and focused; do not refactor unrelated files.
- Schema changes go in a NEW migration file with both Up and Down sections. Never edit a migration that has already been applied.

## Never
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or tokens.
- Never disable tests or security checks to make CI pass.
- Never run destructive commands (`docker compose down -v`, `DROP TABLE`, `git push --force`) without asking.

## Definition of Done
- Tests pass (`npm test` in backend and frontend).
- `docker compose up -d --build` starts cleanly from scratch.
- README updated if setup or commands changed.
